<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Feature Importance</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h3>Feature Importance</h3>
    <p>How much each column tells you about the value you are predicting. Higher means the column carries more signal.</p>
    <p>This is about your data, not about the model you just trained. Train a different algorithm on the same table and you get the same numbers.</p>
    <p>The remaining columns describe the training data itself, so you can spot a column that is nearly always the same value, or one with a suspicious range.</p>
</body>
</html>
